            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0707" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.77a/19: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-15T18:00:00-05:00">October 15, 1930—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>351. Your 905, October 15, noon. Inasmuch as the appointment of a British
                    engineer-in-chief for the Hupeh-Hunan section of the Canton-Hankow Railway is
                    stipulated in Article 17 of the Hukuang Loan <pb facs="0708" n="610"
                        xml:id="pg610"/> Agreement of May 20, 1911, to which the American group is a
                    party, you are authorized to join with the other interested Legations in making
                    identic or similar representations to the Chinese Government concerning the
                    execution of the provisions of the Loan Agreement with respect to the present
                    incumbent as well as concerning the employment of European and/or American
                    engineers-in-chief during the currency of the loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
